:** The property grid updates to show only properties that are available (not fully booked) for the selected date range. The date pickers display the selected dates in a readable format.\n    23→106-\n    24→107-#### Test: Search by guest count filters results\n    25→108-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist with max_guests values of 2, 4, and 8.\n    26→109-- **Action:** User sets the guest count to 5 and clicks the search button.\n    27→110:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where max_guests >= 5. Properties with fewer guest capacity are hidden.\n    28→111-\n    29→112-#### Test: Combined search with all fields filters results\n    30→113-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Multiple properties exist with varying locations, availability, and guest capacities.\n    31→114-- **Action:** User types \"New York\" in the location field, selects check-in \"2026-05-10\" and check-out \"2026-05-15\", sets guests to 3, and clicks the search button.\n    32→115:- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties in New York that are available for those dates and accommodate at least 3 guests.\n    33→116-\n    34→117-#### Test: Clearing search fields and re-searching shows all results\n    35→118-- **Initial state:** User has performed a search for \"Paris\" and the grid shows filtered results.\n    36→119-- **Action:** User clears the location field (making it empty) and clicks the search button.\n    37→120:- **Expected:** The property grid resets to show all properties (unfiltered by location).\n    38→121-\n    39→122-#### Test: Search bar is functional on repeated use\n    40→123-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n    41→124-- **Action:** User searches for \"Paris\", views results, then clears the location field, types \"Tokyo\", and searches again.\n    42→125-- **Expected:** The first search shows only Paris properties. After the second search, the grid updates to show only Tokyo properties. The location input correctly reflects \"Tokyo\".\n    43→--\n    44→146-- **Expected:** A horizontal scrollable bar of category chips is displayed below the search bar. Chips are shown for each property type: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". No chip is selected by default (all properties are shown).\n    45→147-\n    46→148-#### Test: Clicking a category chip filters properties by that type\n    47→149-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of various types exist (apartments, houses, cabins, etc.).\n    48→150-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n    49→151:- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes visually selected/highlighted (e.g., bold outline or filled background). The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Cabin\".\n    50→152-\n    51→153-#### Test: Clicking the selected category chip deselects it and shows all properties\n    52→154-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip currently selected.\n    53→155-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip again.\n    54→156:- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip returns to its unselected appearance. The property grid shows all properties again (no category filter applied).\n    55→157-\n    56→158-#### Test: Switching between category chips updates the filter\n    57→159-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip selected, showing only cabin properties.\n    58→160-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Villa\" chip.\n    59→161:- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes unselected and the \"Villa\" chip becomes selected/highlighted. The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Villa\".\n    60→162-\n    61→163-#### Test: Category filter works in combination with search bar\n    62→164-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist: a cabin in Paris, an apartment in Paris, and a cabin in Tokyo.\n    63→165-- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" in the search bar location field and clicks search, then clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n    64→166:- **Expected:** The property grid shows only cabin properties in Paris. Both the search and category filters are applied simultaneously.\n    65→167-\n    66→168-#### Test: Category filter bar is horizontally scrollable when chips overflow\n    67→169-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page on a narrow viewport where all chips don't fit in one row.\n    68→170-- **Expected:** The category filter bar is horizontally scrollable. The user can scroll left/right to see all property type chips.\n    69→171-\n    70→172-#### Test: Category chip is functional on repeated use\n    71→173-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n    72→174-- **Action:** User clicks \"Apartment\" (filtered), then clicks \"House\" (switches filter), then clicks \"House\" again (deselects), then clicks \"Cabin\" (filtered again).\n    73→175:- **Expected:** Each click correctly updates the selected chip and the property grid filters. The final state shows only cabin properties with the \"Cabin\" chip highlighted.\n    74→176-\n    75→177:### Component: PropertyGrid\n    76→178-\n    77→179-#### Test: Property grid displays properties in a responsive grid layout\n    78→180-- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Multiple properties exist in the database.\n    79→181:- **Expected:** Properties are displayed in a responsive grid: 1 column on mobile, 2 columns on tablet, 3-4 columns on desktop. Each property is rendered as a PropertyCard.\n    80→182-\n    81→183-#### Test: Property grid shows message when no properties match filters\n    82→184-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n    83→185-- **Action:** User searches for a location with no matching properties (e.g., \"Atlantis\").\n    84→186:- **Expected:** The property grid area displays a \"No properties found\" message instead of an empty grid. The message suggests adjusting filters or search criteria.\n    85→187-\n    86→188-#### Test: Property grid loads and displays properties from API on initial page load\n    87→189-- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Properties exist in the database.\n    88→190:- **Expected:** The grid fetches properties via `GET /api/properties` and displays property cards. While loading, a loading indicator is shown. Once loaded, the property cards appear with correct data.\n    89→191-\n    90→192:### Component: PropertyCard\n    91→193-\n    92→194-#### Test: Property card displays all required information\n    93→195-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with title \"Cozy Cabin\", city \"Aspen\", country \"US\", property_type \"Cabin\", price_per_night 150, an average rating of 4.5, and 12 reviews.\n    94→196:- **Expected:** The property card shows: the main property image at the top, a \"Cabin\" property type badge, the title \"Cozy Cabin\", location \"Aspen, US\", \"$150 / night\" price, and a star icon with \"4.5 (12 reviews)\" rating display.\n    95→197-\n    96→198-#### Test: Property card shows property image\n    97→199-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with at least one image (the first image by display_order).\n    98→200:- **Expected:** The property card displays the main image (lowest display_order) at the top of the card with rounded top corners. If no image exists, a placeholder image is shown.\n    99→201-\n   100→202:#### Test: Clicking a property card navigates to property detail page\n   101→203-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property with id \"abc-123\" is displayed.\n   102→204:- **Action:** User clicks on the property card (not the favorite button).\n   103→205-- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page).\n   104→206-\n   105→207-#### Test: Property card displays property type badge\n   106→208-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of different types exist.\n   107→209:- **Expected:** Each property card shows a badge/label indicating the property type (e.g., \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\"). The badge is visually distinct (e.g., small colored label overlaying or near the image).\n   108→210-\n   109→211-#### Test: Property card displays average rating with review count\n   110→212-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property has an average rating of 4.2 from 8 reviews.\n   111→213-- **Expected:** The card shows a star icon with \"4.2\" and \"(8 reviews)\" or \"(8)\" next to it. If the property has no reviews, the rating section shows \"New\" or is not displayed.\n   112→214-\n   113→215-### Component: FavoriteButton\n   114→216-\n   115→217-#### Test: Favorite button shows outline heart when property is not favorited\n   116→218-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. The property is not in the user's favorites.\n   117→219:- **Expected:** The property card displays a heart icon with an outline (unfilled) style in the top-right corner of the card image.\n   118→220-\n   119→221-#### Test: Clicking favorite button on unfavorited property adds it to favorites\n   120→222-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. A property is not in their favorites.\n   121→223:- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on the property card.\n   122→224-- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/favorites` with the property ID. The heart icon changes to a filled/solid red heart. The property is now in the user's favorites list.\n   123→225-\n   124→226-#### Test: Clicking favorite button on favorited property removes it from favorites\n   125→227-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. A property is already in their favorites (heart is filled/red).\n   126→228:- **Action:** User clicks the filled heart icon on the property card.\n   127→229-- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/favorites/:propertyId`. The heart icon changes back to an outline (unfilled) style. The property is removed from the user's favorites.\n   128→230-\n   129→231-#### Test: Favorite button does not navigate to property detail page\n   130→232-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page.\n   131→233:- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on a property card.\n   132→234-- **Expected:** The favorite is toggled but the user remains on the home page. The click does not propagate to the card's navigation handler.\n   133→235-\n   134→236-#### Test: Favorite button is not shown when user is not logged in\n   135→237-- **Initial state:** User is not logged in and is on the home page.\n   136→238-- **Expected:** Property cards do not display the heart/favorite icon. Alternatively, clicking the heart redirects the user to the login page.\n   137→--\n   138→258-- **Expected:** The filters panel opens/expands, revealing all filter controls: a price range slider, bedrooms minimum selector, beds minimum selector, bathrooms minimum selector, and amenity checkboxes grouped by category.\n   139→259-\n   140→260-#### Test: Clicking the Filters button again closes the filters panel\n   141→261-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   142→262-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Filters\" button again.\n   143→263:- **Expected:** The filters panel collapses/hides. The property grid remains showing the previously applied filters.\n   144→264-\n   145→265-#### Test: Price range slider filters properties by price per night\n   146→266-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with prices $50, $100, $200, and $500 per night.\n   147→267-- **Action:** User adjusts the price range slider to a minimum of $75 and a maximum of $250.\n   148→268:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with price_per_night between $75 and $250 (i.e., $100 and $200 properties). The slider visually reflects the selected range with labels showing the min and max values.\n   149→269-\n   150→270-#### Test: Bedrooms minimum filter works correctly\n   151→271-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with 1, 2, 3, and 5 bedrooms.\n   152→272-- **Action:** User sets the bedrooms minimum selector to 3.\n   153→273:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 3 or more bedrooms.\n   154→274-\n   155→275-#### Test: Beds minimum filter works correctly\n   156→276-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with varying bed counts.\n   157→277-- **Action:** User sets the beds minimum selector to 2.\n   158→278:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 2 or more beds.\n   159→279-\n   160→280-#### Test: Bathrooms minimum filter works correctly\n   161→281-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with 1, 2, and 3 bathrooms.\n   162→282-- **Action:** User sets the bathrooms minimum selector to 2.\n   163→283:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 2 or more bathrooms.\n   164→284-\n   165→285-#### Test: Amenity checkboxes filter properties by selected amenities\n   166→286-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Amenities include \"WiFi\", \"Pool\", \"Kitchen\", \"Parking\". Properties have varying amenities.\n   167→287-- **Action:** User checks the \"WiFi\" and \"Pool\" amenity checkboxes.\n   168→288:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that have both WiFi AND Pool amenities. The checked amenities remain visually checked.\n   169→289-\n   170→290-#### Test: Amenity checkboxes are grouped by category\n   171→291-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   172→292-- **Expected:** Amenity checkboxes are organized into groups labeled by category: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each group contains the relevant amenities.\n   173→293-\n   174→294-#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n   175→295-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   176→296-- **Action:** User sets price range to $100–$300, bedrooms minimum to 2, and checks the \"WiFi\" amenity.\n   177→297:- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties that satisfy ALL three conditions: price between $100–$300, at least 2 bedrooms, and has WiFi amenity.\n   178→298-\n   179→299-#### Test: Filters combine with search bar and category filter\n   180→300-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. User has typed \"Paris\" in the search bar, selected \"Apartment\" category chip, and the filters panel is open.\n   181→301-- **Action:** User sets bedrooms minimum to 2 in the filters panel.\n   182→302:- **Expected:** The property grid shows only apartments in Paris with at least 2 bedrooms. All three filter mechanisms (search, category, filters panel) work together.\n   183→303-\n   184→304-#### Test: Resetting filters shows all properties\n   185→305-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with multiple filters applied (price range, bedrooms, amenities).\n   186→306-- **Action:** User resets or clears all filter values back to their defaults (e.g., via a \"Clear Filters\" or \"Reset\" button, or manually resetting each).\n   187→307:- **Expected:** The property grid returns to showing all properties (unfiltered). All filter controls return to their default states.\n   188→308-\n   189→309-#### Test: Filters panel controls are functional on repeated use\n   190→310-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   191→311-- **Action:** User sets bedrooms to 3 (filtered), then changes bedrooms back to 1, then sets bathrooms to 2, then unchecks and re-checks a \"WiFi\" amenity.\n   192→312:- **Expected:** Each change updates the property grid correctly. The final state reflects the last set of filter values (bedrooms >= 1, bathrooms >= 2, WiFi checked).\n   193→313-\n   194→314-### Component: Pagination\n   195→315-\n   196→316-#### Test: Pagination controls are displayed when results exceed one page\n   197→317-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. More properties exist than can fit on one page (e.g., more than the page limit of 12 or 20 properties).\n   198→318:- **Expected:** Pagination controls are displayed below the property grid showing page numbers (e.g., \"1 2 3 ... 5\"), a \"Previous\" button (disabled on first page), and a \"Next\" button.\n   199→319-\n   200→320-#### Test: Pagination controls are hidden when all results fit on one page\n   201→321-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Fewer properties exist than the page limit.\n   202→322:- **Expected:** No pagination controls are displayed below the property grid.\n   203→323-\n   204→324-#### Test: Clicking Next page loads the next set of properties\n   205→325-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page viewing page 1 of results. Multiple pages of properties exist.\n   206→326-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Next\" button.\n   207→327:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the second page of properties. The URL or API call includes `page=2`. The current page indicator highlights \"2\". The \"Previous\" button becomes enabled.\n   208→328-\n   209→329-#### Test: Clicking Previous page loads the previous set of properties\n   210→330-- **Initial state:** User is on page 2 of property results.\n   211→331-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Previous\" button.\n   212→332:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the first page of properties. The current page indicator highlights \"1\". The \"Previous\" button becomes disabled again.\n   213→333-\n   214→334-#### Test: Clicking a specific page number navigates to that page\n   215→335-- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results. At least 3 pages of properties exist.\n   216→336-- **Action:** User clicks page number \"3\".\n   217→337:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the third page of properties. The current page indicator highlights \"3\".\n   218→338-\n   219→339-#### Test: Next button is disabled on the last page\n   220→340-- **Initial state:** User is on the last page of property results.\n   221→341-- **Expected:** The \"Next\" button is disabled/grayed out and not clickable. The \"Previous\" button is enabled.\n   222→342-\n   223→--\n   224→345-- **Expected:** The \"Previous\" button is disabled/grayed out and not clickable. The \"Next\" button is enabled (if more than one page exists).\n   225→346-\n   226→347-#### Test: Applying filters resets pagination to page 1\n   227→348-- **Initial state:** User is on page 3 of property results.\n   228→349-- **Action:** User applies a category filter by clicking the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   229→350:- **Expected:** The pagination resets to page 1. The property grid shows the first page of filtered results. The page indicator highlights \"1\".\n   230→351-\n   231→352-#### Test: Pagination is functional on repeated use\n   232→353-- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results with multiple pages available.\n   233→354-- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\" (goes to page 2), then clicks \"Next\" again (page 3), then clicks \"Previous\" (back to page 2), then clicks page \"1\" (back to page 1).\n   234→355:- **Expected:** Each navigation correctly updates the property grid and page indicator. The final state shows page 1 results.\n   235→356-\n   236→357-## Page: Property Detail (`/properties/:id`)\n   237→358-\n   238→359-<!-- Components: ImageGallery, PropertyHeader, PropertyInfo, PropertyDescription, AmenitiesList, BookingCard, ReviewsSection, HostInfoCard -->\n   239→360-\n   240→--\n   241→798-### Component: ListingsTab\n   242→799-\n   243→800-#### Test: Listings tab displays host's properties in a grid\n   244→801-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 3 active properties: \"Beach House\" ($150/night), \"Mountain Cabin\" ($200/night), \"City Loft\" ($120/night).\n   245→802-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting` (Listings tab is active by default).\n   246→803:- **Expected:** A grid of 3 property cards is displayed. Each card shows the property title, main image, price per night, and status (active/inactive).\n   247→804-\n   248→805-#### Test: Listing card shows property details\n   249→806-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property: title \"Beach House\", price $150/night, city \"Malibu\", 4.5 average rating, 10 reviews, active status.\n   250→807-- **Expected:** The listing card displays the property title \"Beach House\", price \"$150/night\", location \"Malibu\", average rating \"4.5\" with star icon, review count \"10 reviews\", and a green \"Active\" badge.\n   251→808-\n   252→809-#### Test: Listing card has Edit button that navigates to property detail\n   253→810-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property (id \"prop-123\").\n   254→811:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Edit\" button on the property card.\n   255→812-- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/prop-123` where the host can view and edit their property details.\n   256→813-\n   257→814-#### Test: Listing card has Deactivate button for active properties\n   258→815-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an active property \"Beach House\".\n   259→816-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Deactivate\" button on the \"Beach House\" card.\n   260→817-- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Are you sure you want to deactivate this listing?\". The dialog shows the property name \"Beach House\".\n   261→818-\n   262→819-#### Test: Confirming deactivation sets property to inactive\n   263→820-- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n   264→821-- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button (e.g., \"Yes, Deactivate\").\n   265→822:- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/properties/:id` (which sets `is_active` to false). The dialog closes. The property card updates to show an \"Inactive\" status badge (gray or muted). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing deactivated\"). The stats overview updates the \"Total Listings\" count to reflect the change.\n   266→823-\n   267→824-#### Test: Dismissing deactivation dialog keeps property active\n   268→825-- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n   269→826-- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss/cancel button.\n   270→827-- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The property remains active with no changes.\n   271→828-\n   272→829-#### Test: Listing card shows Activate button for inactive properties\n   273→830-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an inactive property \"Old Cabin\".\n   274→831-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Activate\" button on the \"Old Cabin\" card.\n   275→832:- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/properties/:id` to set `is_active` to true. The property card updates to show a green \"Active\" badge. The \"Total Listings\" stat updates.\n   276→833-\n   277→834-#### Test: Listings tab shows empty state for host with no properties\n   278→835-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties.\n   279→836-- **Expected:** The Listings tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You don't have any listings yet\") and a prominent \"Add Listing\" button or call-to-action.\n   280→837-"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0409dc4e-def6-42dd-9dcb-2e7d4bd8a1ac","uuid":"383d4bfb-ae8d-4b40-80f6-cc34d69cc4bc","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/agent/.claude/projects/-repo/0409dc4e-def6-42dd-9dcb-2e7d4bd8a1ac/tool-results/toolu_01X8TZdrMt7WG2D4CWRaXBDS.txt","content":"84-- **Action:** User fills in name and an already-existing email, submits and gets an error, then changes the email to a new unique email and clicks \"Register\" again.\n85-- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is registered and redirected to home.\n86-\n87-## Page: Home / Search (`/`)\n88-\n89:<!-- Components: SearchBar, CategoryFilter, PropertyGrid, PropertyCard, FavoriteButton, FiltersPanel, Pagination -->\n90-\n91-### Component: SearchBar\n92-\n93-#### Test: Search bar displays all input fields on load\n94-- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n95-- **Expected:** The search bar is visible at the top of the page containing four inputs: a location text input with placeholder \"Where are you going?\", a check-in date picker, a check-out date picker, and a guest count selector. A search/submit button with a magnifying glass icon is visible.\n96-\n97-#### Test: Search by location filters property results\n98-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist in \"Paris\", \"New York\", and \"Tokyo\".\n99-- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" into the location input and clicks the search button.\n100:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where the city matches \"Paris\". Properties in other cities are not displayed.\n101-\n102-#### Test: Search by check-in and check-out dates filters results\n103-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Some properties have bookings that overlap with the selected dates.\n104-- **Action:** User selects a check-in date of \"2026-04-01\" and a check-out date of \"2026-04-05\" using the date pickers, then clicks the search button.\n105:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that are available (not fully booked) for the selected date range. The date pickers display the selected dates in a readable format.\n106-\n107-#### Test: Search by guest count filters results\n108-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist with max_guests values of 2, 4, and 8.\n109-- **Action:** User sets the guest count to 5 and clicks the search button.\n110:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where max_guests >= 5. Properties with fewer guest capacity are hidden.\n111-\n112-#### Test: Combined search with all fields filters results\n113-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Multiple properties exist with varying locations, availability, and guest capacities.\n114-- **Action:** User types \"New York\" in the location field, selects check-in \"2026-05-10\" and check-out \"2026-05-15\", sets guests to 3, and clicks the search button.\n115:- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties in New York that are available for those dates and accommodate at least 3 guests.\n116-\n117-#### Test: Clearing search fields and re-searching shows all results\n118-- **Initial state:** User has performed a search for \"Paris\" and the grid shows filtered results.\n119-- **Action:** User clears the location field (making it empty) and clicks the search button.\n120:- **Expected:** The property grid resets to show all properties (unfiltered by location).\n121-\n122-#### Test: Search bar is functional on repeated use\n123-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n124-- **Action:** User searches for \"Paris\", views results, then clears the location field, types \"Tokyo\", and searches again.\n125-- **Expected:** The first search shows only Paris properties. After the second search, the grid updates to show only Tokyo properties. The location input correctly reflects \"Tokyo\".\n--\n146-- **Expected:** A horizontal scrollable bar of category chips is displayed below the search bar. Chips are shown for each property type: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". No chip is selected by default (all properties are shown).\n147-\n148-#### Test: Clicking a category chip filters properties by that type\n149-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of various types exist (apartments, houses, cabins, etc.).\n150-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n151:- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes visually selected/highlighted (e.g., bold outline or filled background). The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Cabin\".\n152-\n153-#### Test: Clicking the selected category chip deselects it and shows all properties\n154-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip currently selected.\n155-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip again.\n156:- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip returns to its unselected appearance. The property grid shows all properties again (no category filter applied).\n157-\n158-#### Test: Switching between category chips updates the filter\n159-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip selected, showing only cabin properties.\n160-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Villa\" chip.\n161:- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes unselected and the \"Villa\" chip becomes selected/highlighted. The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Villa\".\n162-\n163-#### Test: Category filter works in combination with search bar\n164-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist: a cabin in Paris, an apartment in Paris, and a cabin in Tokyo.\n165-- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" in the search bar location field and clicks search, then clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n166:- **Expected:** The property grid shows only cabin properties in Paris. Both the search and category filters are applied simultaneously.\n167-\n168-#### Test: Category filter bar is horizontally scrollable when chips overflow\n169-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page on a narrow viewport where all chips don't fit in one row.\n170-- **Expected:** The category filter bar is horizontally scrollable. The user can scroll left/right to see all property type chips.\n171-\n172-#### Test: Category chip is functional on repeated use\n173-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n174-- **Action:** User clicks \"Apartment\" (filtered), then clicks \"House\" (switches filter), then clicks \"House\" again (deselects), then clicks \"Cabin\" (filtered again).\n175:- **Expected:** Each click correctly updates the selected chip and the property grid filters. The final state shows only cabin properties with the \"Cabin\" chip highlighted.\n176-\n177:### Component: PropertyGrid\n178-\n179-#### Test: Property grid displays properties in a responsive grid layout\n180-- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Multiple properties exist in the database.\n181:- **Expected:** Properties are displayed in a responsive grid: 1 column on mobile, 2 columns on tablet, 3-4 columns on desktop. Each property is rendered as a PropertyCard.\n182-\n183-#### Test: Property grid shows message when no properties match filters\n184-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n185-- **Action:** User searches for a location with no matching properties (e.g., \"Atlantis\").\n186:- **Expected:** The property grid area displays a \"No properties found\" message instead of an empty grid. The message suggests adjusting filters or search criteria.\n187-\n188-#### Test: Property grid loads and displays properties from API on initial page load\n189-- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Properties exist in the database.\n190:- **Expected:** The grid fetches properties via `GET /api/properties` and displays property cards. While loading, a loading indicator is shown. Once loaded, the property cards appear with correct data.\n191-\n192:### Component: PropertyCard\n193-\n194-#### Test: Property card displays all required information\n195-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with title \"Cozy Cabin\", city \"Aspen\", country \"US\", property_type \"Cabin\", price_per_night 150, an average rating of 4.5, and 12 reviews.\n196:- **Expected:** The property card shows: the main property image at the top, a \"Cabin\" property type badge, the title \"Cozy Cabin\", location \"Aspen, US\", \"$150 / night\" price, and a star icon with \"4.5 (12 reviews)\" rating display.\n197-\n198-#### Test: Property card shows property image\n199-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with at least one image (the first image by display_order).\n200:- **Expected:** The property card displays the main image (lowest display_order) at the top of the card with rounded top corners. If no image exists, a placeholder image is shown.\n201-\n202:#### Test: Clicking a property card navigates to property detail page\n203-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property with id \"abc-123\" is displayed.\n204:- **Action:** User clicks on the property card (not the favorite button).\n205-- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page).\n206-\n207-#### Test: Property card displays property type badge\n208-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of different types exist.\n209:- **Expected:** Each property card shows a badge/label indicating the property type (e.g., \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\"). The badge is visually distinct (e.g., small colored label overlaying or near the image).\n210-\n211-#### Test: Property card displays average rating with review count\n212-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property has an average rating of 4.2 from 8 reviews.\n213-- **Expected:** The card shows a star icon with \"4.2\" and \"(8 reviews)\" or \"(8)\" next to it. If the property has no reviews, the rating section shows \"New\" or is not displayed.\n214-\n215-### Component: FavoriteButton\n216-\n217-#### Test: Favorite button shows outline heart when property is not favorited\n218-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. The property is not in the user's favorites.\n219:- **Expected:** The property card displays a heart icon with an outline (unfilled) style in the top-right corner of the card image.\n220-\n221-#### Test: Clicking favorite button on unfavorited property adds it to favorites\n222-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. A property is not in their favorites.\n223:- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on the property card.\n224-- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/favorites` with the property ID. The heart icon changes to a filled/solid red heart. The property is now in the user's favorites list.\n225-\n226-#### Test: Clicking favorite button on favorited property removes it from favorites\n227-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. A property is already in their favorites (heart is filled/red).\n228:- **Action:** User clicks the filled heart icon on the property card.\n229-- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/favorites/:propertyId`. The heart icon changes back to an outline (unfilled) style. The property is removed from the user's favorites.\n230-\n231-#### Test: Favorite button does not navigate to property detail page\n232-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page.\n233:- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on a property card.\n234-- **Expected:** The favorite is toggled but the user remains on the home page. The click does not propagate to the card's navigation handler.\n235-\n236-#### Test: Favorite button is not shown when user is not logged in\n237-- **Initial state:** User is not logged in and is on the home page.\n238-- **Expected:** Property cards do not display the heart/favorite icon. Alternatively, clicking the heart redirects the user to the login page.\n--\n258-- **Expected:** The filters panel opens/expands, revealing all filter controls: a price range slider, bedrooms minimum selector, beds minimum selector, bathrooms minimum selector, and amenity checkboxes grouped by category.\n259-\n260-#### Test: Clicking the Filters button again closes the filters panel\n261-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n262-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Filters\" button again.\n263:- **Expected:** The filters panel collapses/hides. The property grid remains showing the previously applied filters.\n264-\n265-#### Test: Price range slider filters properties by price per night\n266-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with prices $50, $100, $200, and $500 per night.\n267-- **Action:** User adjusts the price range slider to a minimum of $75 and a maximum of $250.\n268:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with price_per_night between $75 and $250 (i.e., $100 and $200 properties). The slider visually reflects the selected range with labels showing the min and max values.\n269-\n270-#### Test: Bedrooms minimum filter works correctly\n271-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with 1, 2, 3, and 5 bedrooms.\n272-- **Action:** User sets the bedrooms minimum selector to 3.\n273:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 3 or more bedrooms.\n274-\n275-#### Test: Beds minimum filter works correctly\n276-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with varying bed counts.\n277-- **Action:** User sets the beds minimum selector to 2.\n278:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 2 or more beds.\n279-\n280-#### Test: Bathrooms minimum filter works correctly\n281-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with 1, 2, and 3 bathrooms.\n282-- **Action:** User sets the bathrooms minimum selector to 2.\n283:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 2 or more bathrooms.\n284-\n285-#### Test: Amenity checkboxes filter properties by selected amenities\n286-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Amenities include \"WiFi\", \"Pool\", \"Kitchen\", \"Parking\". Properties have varying amenities.\n287-- **Action:** User checks the \"WiFi\" and \"Pool\" amenity checkboxes.\n288:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that have both WiFi AND Pool amenities. The checked amenities remain visually checked.\n289-\n290-#### Test: Amenity checkboxes are grouped by category\n291-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n292-- **Expected:** Amenity checkboxes are organized into groups labeled by category: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each group contains the relevant amenities.\n293-\n294-#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n295-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n296-- **Action:** User sets price range to $100–$300, bedrooms minimum to 2, and checks the \"WiFi\" amenity.\n297:- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties that satisfy ALL three conditions: price between $100–$300, at least 2 bedrooms, and has WiFi amenity.\n298-\n299-#### Test: Filters combine with search bar and category filter\n300-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. User has typed \"Paris\" in the search bar, selected \"Apartment\" category chip, and the filters panel is open.\n301-- **Action:** User sets bedrooms minimum to 2 in the filters panel.\n302:- **Expected:** The property grid shows only apartments in Paris with at least 2 bedrooms. All three filter mechanisms (search, category, filters panel) work together.\n303-\n304-#### Test: Resetting filters shows all properties\n305-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with multiple filters applied (price range, bedrooms, amenities).\n306-- **Action:** User resets or clears all filter values back to their defaults (e.g., via a \"Clear Filters\" or \"Reset\" button, or manually resetting each).\n307:- **Expected:** The property grid returns to showing all properties (unfiltered). All filter controls return to their default states.\n308-\n309-#### Test: Filters panel controls are functional on repeated use\n310-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n311-- **Action:** User sets bedrooms to 3 (filtered), then changes bedrooms back to 1, then sets bathrooms to 2, then unchecks and re-checks a \"WiFi\" amenity.\n312:- **Expected:** Each change updates the property grid correctly. The final state reflects the last set of filter values (bedrooms >= 1, bathrooms >= 2, WiFi checked).\n313-\n314-### Component: Pagination\n315-\n316-#### Test: Pagination controls are displayed when results exceed one page\n317-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. More properties exist than can fit on one page (e.g., more than the page limit of 12 or 20 properties).\n318:- **Expected:** Pagination controls are displayed below the property grid showing page numbers (e.g., \"1 2 3 ... 5\"), a \"Previous\" button (disabled on first page), and a \"Next\" button.\n319-\n320-#### Test: Pagination controls are hidden when all results fit on one page\n321-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Fewer properties exist than the page limit.\n322:- **Expected:** No pagination controls are displayed below the property grid.\n323-\n324-#### Test: Clicking Next page loads the next set of properties\n325-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page viewing page 1 of results. Multiple pages of properties exist.\n326-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Next\" button.\n327:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the second page of properties. The URL or API call includes `page=2`. The current page indicator highlights \"2\". The \"Previous\" button becomes enabled.\n328-\n329-#### Test: Clicking Previous page loads the previous set of properties\n330-- **Initial state:** User is on page 2 of property results.\n331-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Previous\" button.\n332:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the first page of properties. The current page indicator highlights \"1\". The \"Previous\" button becomes disabled again.\n333-\n334-#### Test: Clicking a specific page number navigates to that page\n335-- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results. At least 3 pages of properties exist.\n336-- **Action:** User clicks page number \"3\".\n337:- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the third page of properties. The current page indicator highlights \"3\".\n338-\n339-#### Test: Next button is disabled on the last page\n340-- **Initial state:** User is on the last page of property results.\n341-- **Expected:** The \"Next\" button is disabled/grayed out and not clickable. The \"Previous\" button is enabled.\n342-\n--\n345-- **Expected:** The \"Previous\" button is disabled/grayed out and not clickable. The \"Next\" button is enabled (if more than one page exists).\n346-\n347-#### Test: Applying filters resets pagination to page 1\n348-- **Initial state:** User is on page 3 of property results.\n349-- **Action:** User applies a category filter by clicking the \"Cabin\" chip.\n350:- **Expected:** The pagination resets to page 1. The property grid shows the first page of filtered results. The page indicator highlights \"1\".\n351-\n352-#### Test: Pagination is functional on repeated use\n353-- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results with multiple pages available.\n354-- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\" (goes to page 2), then clicks \"Next\" again (page 3), then clicks \"Previous\" (back to page 2), then clicks page \"1\" (back to page 1).\n355:- **Expected:** Each navigation correctly updates the property grid and page indicator. The final state shows page 1 results.\n356-\n357-## Page: Property Detail (`/properties/:id`)\n358-\n359-<!-- Components: ImageGallery, PropertyHeader, PropertyInfo, PropertyDescription, AmenitiesList, BookingCard, ReviewsSection, HostInfoCard -->\n360-\n--\n798-### Component: ListingsTab\n799-\n800-#### Test: Listings tab displays host's properties in a grid\n801-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 3 active properties: \"Beach House\" ($150/night), \"Mountain Cabin\" ($200/night), \"City Loft\" ($120/night).\n802-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting` (Listings tab is active by default).\n803:- **Expected:** A grid of 3 property cards is displayed. Each card shows the property title, main image, price per night, and status (active/inactive).\n804-\n805-#### Test: Listing card shows property details\n806-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property: title \"Beach House\", price $150/night, city \"Malibu\", 4.5 average rating, 10 reviews, active status.\n807-- **Expected:** The listing card displays the property title \"Beach House\", price \"$150/night\", location \"Malibu\", average rating \"4.5\" with star icon, review count \"10 reviews\", and a green \"Active\" badge.\n808-\n809-#### Test: Listing card has Edit button that navigates to property detail\n810-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property (id \"prop-123\").\n811:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Edit\" button on the property card.\n812-- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/prop-123` where the host can view and edit their property details.\n813-\n814-#### Test: Listing card has Deactivate button for active properties\n815-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an active property \"Beach House\".\n816-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Deactivate\" button on the \"Beach House\" card.\n817-- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Are you sure you want to deactivate this listing?\". The dialog shows the property name \"Beach House\".\n818-\n819-#### Test: Confirming deactivation sets property to inactive\n820-- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n821-- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button (e.g., \"Yes, Deactivate\").\n822:- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/properties/:id` (which sets `is_active` to false). The dialog closes. The property card updates to show an \"Inactive\" status badge (gray or muted). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing deactivated\"). The stats overview updates the \"Total Listings\" count to reflect the change.\n823-\n824-#### Test: Dismissing deactivation dialog keeps property active\n825-- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n826-- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss/cancel button.\n827-- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The property remains active with no changes.\n828-\n829-#### Test: Listing card shows Activate button for inactive properties\n830-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an inactive property \"Old Cabin\".\n831-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Activate\" button on the \"Old Cabin\" card.\n832:- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/properties/:id` to set `is_active` to true. The property card updates to show a green \"Active\" badge. The \"Total Listings\" stat updates.\n833-\n834-#### Test: Listings tab shows empty state for host with no properties\n835-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties.\n836-- **Expected:** The Listings tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You don't have any listings yet\") and a prominent \"Add Listing\" button or call-to-action.\n837-","numLines":280,"startLine":1,"totalLines":280}}}
